WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.046
The Wall opened by mistake.

00:00:02.071 --> 00:00:04.070
One muddled answer started it.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.488
November 9th, 1989.

00:00:05.498 --> 00:00:09.459
East German official
Günter Schabowski is handed

00:00:09.469 --> 00:00:11.889
a note about new travel rules.

00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:13.520
They're meant to start the next day,

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.665
with visas.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:17.080
At a press conference, a reporter asks:

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:17.814
when?

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:18.788
He answers:

00:00:18.798 --> 00:00:20.324
effective immediately.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.599
West German TV reports that the Wall

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:23.609
is open.

00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:25.671
Crowds head for the crossings.

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:28.896
At one gate, officer
Harald Jäger's superior

00:00:28.906 --> 00:00:30.845
tells him to turn people away.

00:00:30.855 --> 00:00:33.126
At 11:30 that night, with no orders,

00:00:33.136 --> 00:00:34.722
he lets them through.
